        "Myeloma: older adults, CRAB — hypercalcaemia, renal failure, anaemia, bone pain, lytic lesions, pathological fractures and cord compression — plus infections, high ESR, rouleaux and Bence Jones protein; nursing is three litres of fluid a day, no NSAIDs or contrast, careful handling, bisphosphonates, thromboprophylaxis with thalidomide, infection vigilance and treating back pain with leg weakness or bladder symptoms as cord compression. Bone marrow biopsy: posterior iliac crest, consent and platelet check, pressure dressing, lie on the site 15–30 minutes, observe for bleeding.",
        "Febrile neutropenia — a single temperature of 38 °C (or 37.5 twice) or an unwell neutropenic patient without fever — means blood cultures from every lumen and broad-spectrum intravenous antibiotics within 60 minutes without waiting for the count; there may be no pus or redness; no rectal temperature; test for malaria; sepsis is three out (cultures, lactate, urine output) and three in (oxygen, fluids, antibiotics) and blood pressure falls late.",
        "Tumour lysis (Burkitt, high-count leukaemia): high potassium, phosphate and uric acid, low calcium, kidney injury — prevented by hyperhydration from 24–48 hours before, allopurinol or rasburicase, no potassium in fluids and 6–12-hourly electrolytes; cord compression — flat, log-roll, urgent dexamethasone and imaging; SVC obstruction — sit up, oxygen, no arm cannulas, urgent treatment; hypercalcaemia — saline then bisphosphonate; hyperviscosity — no red cells until the count is lowered; promyelocytic DIC — all-trans retinoic acid and blood products.",
        "Chemotherapy is dosed in mg/m² from a height and weight measured every cycle, adjusted for organ function and today's counts, and independently double-checked by two trained nurses (patient, protocol, cycle, drug, dose, route, rate, cumulative dose, counts, premedication, consent). Only methotrexate, cytarabine and hydrocortisone are ever given intrathecally; vincristine intrathecally is fatal, so it is prepared in a minibag, labelled, and kept away from lumbar punctures. Watch doxorubicin's cumulative cardiotoxicity, cyclophosphamide's haemorrhagic cystitis (mesna, hydration, voiding), vincristine's constipation and neuropathy (laxatives), methotrexate's interactions (no NSAIDs, trimethoprim or penicillins; folinic acid on time), L-asparaginase anaphylaxis and pancreatitis, cisplatin's kidneys and ears, thalidomide's teratogenicity and clots, rituximab's first-infusion reactions.",
        "Cytotoxics are reconstituted in a safety cabinet, given with double gloves, gown and eye protection by trained non-pregnant staff, disposed of as purple cytotoxic waste, and spills cleaned with the cytotoxic kit; the patient's excreta are hazardous for 48 hours (double flush, lid down, gloves, separate linen). Prevent extravasation with a fresh forearm cannula, confirmed blood return and central access for vesicants; if it happens, stop, aspirate through the cannula, do not flush, mark and elevate, cold for anthracyclines and warm for vinca alkaloids, antidote by protocol, report and review daily.",
        "Through the nadir (7–14 days): hand hygiene by everyone, four-hourly temperature with fever an emergency, daily mouth, skin, perineum and line checks, no rectal route, no intramuscular injections, no flowers or standing water, cooked food only — no raw salads, unpeeled fruit, soft cheese or street food — no live vaccines, co-trimoxazole and antifungal prophylaxis as prescribed; saline mouthwash two- to four-hourly and soft bland food with morphine for severe mucositis; antiemetics before the drug; alopecia, fertility and contraception discussed before the first dose; aseptic central line care with weekly dressings and cultures for any fever. In Ghana abandonment of treatment is the leading cause of death in childhood cancer — NHIS enrolment, social work, recorded phone numbers, missed appointments chased, healers engaged alongside treatment; when cure is not possible, oral morphine, symptom control, honest conversation and spiritual care.",
